Proposed patch for protected .claude/hooks files (docs/architecture.md section 7.1).
Prepared by Claude Code on 2026-10-21; NOT applied (Claude Code cannot edit .claude/).
Fixes the 6 extended-rule lint findings and the hook formatting:
  - EXE001 x2: remove shebangs (both hooks are invoked as `python3 <file>`; no exec bit needed)
  - BLE001 (hook main): broad except is deliberate (fail closed) -> justified noqa
  - SIM105 + BLE001 (session_note): contextlib.suppress with specific exceptions
  - ruff format: 3 cosmetic hunks in block_model_execution.py
Behaviour is unchanged: the hook still exits 2 on any internal error.
Apply from the repository root, then run the hook tests:
  git apply --check docs/proposed_patches/2026-10-21_hook_lint_format.patch
  git apply docs/proposed_patches/2026-10-21_hook_lint_format.patch
  ruff check .claude/hooks --extend-select EXE,BLE,SIM,RUF100 && ruff format --check .claude/hooks
  PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m pytest tests/test_safety_hooks.py -q

